    skos:definition "In Commerce, the grains of several species of *gramina*. Those of most importance are clover seed, flax or linseed, hemp seed, rape seed, tares, mustard seed &c.; for which, see the respective articles. But it may be useful to subjoin the following *Account of the Imports and Exports of the Principal Seeds in 1867.* The total value of the seeds imported in 1867 was 6,918,433*l.* SEGARS or CIGARS. [TOBACCO.] SENNA (Fr. *séné*; Ger. *sennablätter*; Ital. *senna*; Span. *sen*;... [J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1352]"@en ;
