    oe:isAggregate "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:definition "a commercial weight varying with the article weighed, but legally 14 lbs. The stone of butcher's meat or fish is usually reckoned at 8 lbs.; of cheese 16 lbs.; of hemp 32 lbs.; of glass 5 lbs. In Hamburg a stone of flax is 20 lbs.; of feathers 10 lbs. The Prussian stone of 22 lbs. is equal to 22 $\\frac{1}{2}$ lbs. avoirdupois, 5 stone making 1 trade centner, of 110 lbs. = 113 lbs. avoirdupois, nearly. \\* [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 374]"@en ;
    oe:dictionarySource <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n374>, <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
