    skos:definition "(GER. *Schwefel*. DU. *Zwafel*, *Zolfer*. DA. *Suovel*. SW. *Swafuel*. FR. *Soufre*. IT. *Zolfo*, *Solfo*. SP. *Azufre*. PORT. *Enxofre*. RUS. *Sjera*. POL. *Siarka*. LAT. *Sulphur*.) See SULPHUR. *Brimstone medals*, figures, &c. may be cast from a composition consisting of equal weights of sulphur and vermilion melted together. When cleared the composition may be cast in a mould smeared with oil. If it should change to a yellowish hue, wet it with aqua-fortis, and it will... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 178]"@en ;
