    oe:isAggregate "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:definition "(_Outremer_, Fr.; _Ultramarins_, Germ.); is a beautiful blue pigment obtained from the variegated blue mineral, called lazulite (_lapis lazuli_), by the following process:--Grind the stone to fragments, rejecting all the colourless bits, calcine at a red heat, quench in water, and then grind to an impalpable powder along with water, in a paint-mill, (see PAINTS, GRINDING OF,) or with a porphyry slab and muller. [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]"@en ;
    oe:dictionarySource <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562>, <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n406> ;
