    skos:definition "(GER. and DU. *Tamarinden*. DA. *Tamerin*. SW. *Tamarind*. FR. *Tamarins*. IT. and SP. *Tamarindo*. PORT. *Tamarinho*. LAT. *Tamarindus*,) the fruit of the *tamarindus indica*. It is a pod resembling a beancod, including several hard seeds, together with a dark-coloured viscid pulp, of a pleasant acid taste: the East India tamarinds are longer than the West India sort; the former containing six or seven seeds each, the latter rarely above three or four. Tamarinds are... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 955]"@en ;
