    skos:definition "(GER. *Grünspan*. DU. *Spaansch groen*. DA. *Spansk grønt*. SW. *Spank gröna*. FR. *Verde-gris*, *Verdet*. IT. *Verderame*. SP. *Cardenillo*, *Verdete*, *Verde-gris*. PORT. *Verdete*, *Verdegris*, *Cardinillo*. RUS. *Jar*. POL. *Gryszpan*. LAT. *Ærugo*, *Viride æris*,) is an acetat of copper, useful in the arts as a pigment. The principles on which it is formed are these : Acetic acid attacks copper very slowly in open vessels, converts it into an oxide, and dissolves it;... [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 980]"@en ;
